The HIP²LInterActomics graphical interface uses PyQt6.

PyQt6 is distributed by Riverbank Computing Limited under the GNU General
Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0-only), or under a separate commercial
license for appropriately licensed users.

The publicly distributed open-source builds of HIP²LInterActomics use the
GPL-licensed version of PyQt6. Accordingly, the HIP²LInterActomics desktop
application is distributed under GPL-3.0-only.

Qt libraries distributed as dependencies of PyQt6 retain their respective
Qt licensing terms, including applicable GNU Lesser General Public License
(LGPL) and/or other licenses.

Nothing in this file relicenses PyQt6, Qt, or any other third-party
component.


4. Scientific Computation Environment
-------------------------------------

HIP²LInterActomics separates its graphical/interface environment from the
scientific computation environment used for molecular analysis.

The scientific environment ("luna-env") may contain or invoke independent
third-party software including, but not limited to:

    LUNA
    RDKit
    Open Babel
    PyMOL Open Source
    Biopython
    NumPy
    SciPy
    pandas
    scikit-learn
    Matplotlib
    NetworkX
    and their dependencies.

These components retain their respective licenses.

In particular:

    LUNA
        Distributed under its upstream open-source license.

    RDKit
        Distributed under its upstream BSD-style license.

    Open Babel
        Distributed under the GNU General Public License version 2
        according to its upstream licensing terms.

    PyMOL Open Source
        Distributed under its upstream open-source license.

    NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, pandas, NetworkX, Biopython,
    Matplotlib, and related scientific libraries
        Distributed under their respective upstream open-source licenses.

Users redistributing these components are responsible for complying with
the corresponding upstream license terms.


5. Separation of HIP²LInterActomics and External Scientific Programs
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Some scientific programs are executed by HIP²LInterActomics as independent
processes through command-line interfaces, subprocess execution, files,
configuration files, or serialized project data.

In particular, components installed inside the separate "luna-env"
environment are not automatically relicensed as part of HIP²LInterActomics.

For example, HIP²LInterActomics may invoke the Open Babel command-line
program ("obabel") as an external process. Open Babel remains governed by
its own license.

Likewise, LUNA, RDKit, PyMOL, and other components installed in the
scientific environment retain their respective copyright and licensing
terms.


6. PyInstaller and Packaging Tools
----------------------------------

Desktop distributions of HIP²LInterActomics may be created using
PyInstaller and additional packaging tools such as Inno Setup and
AppImage tooling.

These build and packaging tools retain their respective licenses.

The use of these tools to create HIP²LInterActomics distributions does not
transfer ownership of those tools to the HIP²LInterActomics authors and
does not supersede their upstream licensing conditions.


7. Third-Party Components Included in Binary Distributions
